+# Q3 revenue drop
+
+East had the largest Q2→Q3 revenue fall of any region: −29.79%, from 333,747.57 to 234,325.08 (−99,422.49). North was next at −4.33%. Ledger Pro accounts for most of East's drop: its revenue went from 106,520.77 to 23,015.24 (−83,505.53, about 84% of the region's loss). Unit prices and refunds stayed flat. The fall comes from volume: East's completed Ledger Pro orders dropped from about 100 a month to about 25 a month in July–September, then recovered in October. Revenue is units × unit_price over `completed` rows only, with refunds (negative units) included. Note that the export has completed rows dated through 2026-12-31, after the date of this report, so the Q4 figure should be checked before anyone relies on it.
+
+| Quarter | East revenue |
+|---------|-------------:|
+| Q1      |   333,565.48 |
+| Q2      |   333,747.57 |
+| Q3      |   234,325.08 |
+| Q4      |   305,168.76 |
